<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Convention People's Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1949">1949</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as CPP</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Convention People's Party is a Ghanaian political party founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwame-nkrumah">Kwame Nkrumah</a> in June 1949 after he broke with the United <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-coast">Gold Coast</a> Convention. Demanding 'self-government now', it won the elections of 1951, 1954 and 1956, led the Gold Coast to independence as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a> in 1957 and became the only legal party in 1964, until the coup of 1966 overthrew Nkrumah.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/convention-peoples-party.jpg" alt="Convention People's Party" width="295" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Convention People's Party (CPP) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CPP_%E2%80%92_Convention_People%27s_Party_logo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
